Troubleshooting
pgAudit fails to load: confirm shared_preload_libraries matches installed version path; restart service after any config change.
Role login fails: check pg_hba.conf allows password authentication for local connections (md5 or scram-sha-256).
RLS not restricting rows: confirm ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY was run and no BYPASSRLS privilege was granted to the role.
Conclusion
In this lab, you implemented a need-to-know access model on a PostgreSQL database by creating distinct roles for HR, finance, and audit functions. You applied column-level and row-level security to restrict data visibility according to job function, enabled pgAudit to capture access attempts for accountability, and validated segregation of duties by impersonating each role. Finally, you documented how these technical controls align with PDPL principles of data minimization, purpose limitation, and accountability. These skills are directly applicable to database administration and security engineering roles responsible for enforcing least privilege in regulated, multi-agency data environments.
